Z||000000||WisconsinGT||02-26-2000||11:30 PM||||I have just installed a new IAC valve. My problem is...that when I start my 88GT up, it idels at 21000 2200 RPM's. What did I do wrong? Also, I now that the IAC valve Pintel was pushed in before I put it in. It is an ACDelco by the way. <P>A funny yet almost serious story. I also bought the decarb kit from my local GM dealer. So I took out the old IAC valve, un-hooked the rubber piece that connects the air cleaner to the throttle body. I sprayed the can that cleans the throttle body into it. Then I put in the new IAC valve. I also installed Rodney Dickmans Tach filter. I wait awhile thinking that the cleaner I used would need some time to evaporate. I then start the car. It idels high. I wait awhile in hopes that it just needs to warm up. Not the case. Instead, the crossover pipe starts on fire. I blow like I have never blowen before. The fire goes out. Should I be concerned when I start the car tomorrow? I want to think that the fluid I used will evaporate. No? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||02-27-2000||12:13 AM||||The computer resets the IAC when you drive 30 or 35 mph after a few minutes.  I know someone else will have the exact mph.  ||||reg||1
